        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8429134e-3f30-504e-a958-c9b00f1087e7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marcia Wallace, Edna Krabappel, David Silverman, Dan Castellaneta, Julie Kavner, Nancy Cartwright, Yeardley Smith, Hank Azaria, Harry Shearer, Tress MacNeille, Pamela Hayden, Maggie Roswell, Russi Taylor, Tom Hanks, Albert Brooks\n- Works: The Bob Newhart Show, The Simpsons, The Simpsons Movie\n- Roles: Carol Kester, Edna Krabappel\n- Organizations: Springfield Elementary School, Green Day\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1970s, Marcia Wallace played receptionist Carol Kester on the sitcom The Bob Newhart Show.\n- In 1992, Marcia Wallace won an Emmy for voicing elementary school teacher Edna Krabappel on The Simpsons.\n- Edna Krabappel is Bart Simpson's fourth-grade teacher at Springfield Elementary School in The Simpsons.\n- In later seasons of The Simpsons, Edna Krabappel becomes Ned Flanders's wife.\n- The Simpsons Movie was directed by David Silverman.\n- The Simpsons Movie features the regular television cast including Dan Castellaneta, Julie Kavner, Nancy Cartwright, Yeardley Smith, Hank Azaria, Harry Shearer, Tress MacNeille, Pamela Hayden, Marcia Wallace, Maggie Roswell, and Russi Taylor.\n- The Simpsons Movie also features Tom Hanks, Green Day, and Albert Brooks.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
